    "body": "Closes #953.\n\n## What changed\n\n- preserve the frozen #989 `SFTBL001` bytes and predictor;\n- add the separate, canonically serialized `MultiscaleCountRadiusR4V1` overlay bound to the base-table CID;\n- compare disabled and geometric choices from one shared active-row computation with exact token-support equality and a shared declared-operation ledger;\n- add the research CLI/report surface, focused natural preflight, and append-only evidence record; and\n- reconcile the programme authority so #973 becomes next only after this protected closure.\n\n## Frozen decision-bearing result\n\n- baseline: 99,362/446,342 = 22.261404%;\n- geometric: 103,604/446,342 = 23.211797%;\n- increment: +4,242 correct, +0.950392 percentage points;\n- changed choices: 56,280, with 6,753 geometric-correct vs 2,511 baseline-correct;\n- reachable maximum-count ties: 76,641/446,342;\n- candidate-support mismatches: 0;\n- declared-work-ledger mismatches: 0;\n- structural teacher/provider/source-weight/held-out-fit counters: 0; and\n- first decoded divergence: emitted unit 12, with equal support and declared-work ledger through that shared frame.\n\nThe disabled continuation remained:\n\n```text\n. It is the most important thing to do so.\n 1985 – The first people\n```\n\nThe geometric continuation became:\n\n```text\n. It is the most important thing to do so. The first people to live\n```\n\nBoth emitted 16 valid UTF-8 lexical units and stopped at the cap without a period-1/2 cycle.\n\nEach JSON report retained `PROCEED_TO_A1Q_H_PENDING_BYTE_IDENTICAL_REPLAY`. External exact comparison of the two complete executions promoted that pending verdict to the frozen terminal `PROCEED_TO_A1Q_H_WITH_BOUNDED_SOURCE_FREE_GEOMETRIC_GENERATION`.\n\n## Frozen artifacts and replay\n\n- base table CID: `blake3:ccdc399731cb866a329be478467a434cda4e445813421e5d17c21ccc87288297` (unchanged #989 artifact);\n- overlay CID: `blake3:914126a311c3984d1482258a8f0a7fa2e34896540d502d19f1d9076fbd4a9b76`;\n- report payload CID: `blake3:0234eec7aa8087962b74497dd3df591e6bfb9bf197e84595292948254d30c7fe`;\n- complete report SHA-256, both runs: `8975c8271d9ba6ee23e6f8e66a2c4902636bba446a8f89075e2495e9341e01a3`;\n- first run: 615.00 s including build; and\n- already-built replay: 577.28 s.\n\n## Activated evidence\n\n- frozen natural #953 preflight: 3/3;\n- unchanged #989 regression: 3/3;\n- focused `uor-r4-core` and `r4` compilation: clean;\n- focused CLI parser check: 1/1;\n- Rust formatting, diff whitespace, and claim-wording gate: clean; and\n- two complete frozen corpus executions: byte-identical and positive.\n\nAllocation-free/deployed-serving behavior, runtime performance, workspace-wide tests/clippy, BDD, teacher/model paths, no-std, Gate C, kappa, audit, fuzz, conformance, product, formal, and release qualification remain `NOT_RUN`, not PASS. The required queue contexts are transport acknowledgements, not QA evidence.\n\nThis establishes only a bounded source-free fixed-point R4 count-radius increment over the frozen lexical table. It does not establish semantic geometry, broad attention, general coherence, correctness, reasoning, chat quality, performance superiority, formal closure, or release readiness.\n",
